(`free`, `release`, and `deallocate` all fold to Token::Free in the lexer,
 and each accepts an optional `the` - `Release the data.` used to be a
 compile error because `parse_free` did not skip it the way
 `parse_increment` does. All three spellings, with and without the article,
 behave identically.)

a buffer called first is "one".
Release the first.
Print "first len {first's length}".

a buffer called second is "two".
Deallocate second.
Print "second len {second's length}".

a buffer called third is "three".
Free third.
Print "third len {third's length}".
